# Template punctuation

Every template in `src/templates/` (including subfolders) follows these rules. They apply to **visible
text and to comments alike**: Jinja comments (`{# … #}`), HTML comments (`<!-- … -->`) and
attribute text (`title`, `aria-label`, `alt`, `placeholder`, `<meta name="description">`).

When you add or edit a template, fix the punctuation of anything you touch, and check the whole file
before committing (see *Checking* below).

## Dashes: only where needed, and the right one

| Mark | Use it for | Never for |
|------|-----------|-----------|
| **Hyphen** `-` | Compound words and modifiers: `waiting-room`, `sign-in`, `number-only`, `walk-in`. | A pause or break in a sentence. A spaced hyphen (` - `) is never correct in prose. |
| **En dash** `–` | Ranges: `~15–25 min`, `#1–#8`, `weeks 11–14`, `$45–80`. No spaces around it. | Anything that is not a range. |
| **Em dash** `—` | A placeholder that means "no value": `{{ user.last_login or '—' }}`, a "nothing selected" option such as `<option value="">— verb —</option>`, an empty table cell. | Joining clauses, introducing an explanation, or wrapping an aside. Use the marks below instead. |

Do not use `--` as a dash anywhere.

**Exception:** text that reproduces machine output verbatim keeps that system's characters. The
USSD transcript on the landing page is GSM 7-bit ASCII, so `2.4km - 6 waiting` and `15-25 min` stay
as they are; say so in a comment next to it.

## What to use instead of a dash

- **Colon** `:` when what follows explains, lists or names what came before.
  `Uses only existing shell classes: no inline styles or handlers.`
- **Semicolon** `;` to join two complete clauses that belong together.
  `This is a read; nothing is changed and nothing is recorded.`
- **Comma** `,` for a light aside or a contrast.
  `Reason text and visit notes are deleted automatically after a short window, with a test that proves they are gone.`
- **Parentheses** `( )` for a true aside or a citation.
  `Some records (the audit trail, and clinical records the clinic must keep by law) cannot be erased.`
  `Performance of the service you asked for (s11(1)(b))`
- **Full stop** `.` when the sentence is doing two jobs: split it.
- **Question mark** `?` for a real question, including in headings and FAQ text.

## Quotes, apostrophes and ellipses

- Straight quotes only: `'` for apostrophes (`it's`, `clinic's`) and `"` for quoted speech. No curly
  quotes (`“ ” ‘ ’`): mixing the two styles is what this rule exists to prevent.
- An ellipsis (`…`) only for a genuine omission or trailing off. Code notation such as `can(...)` or
  `'nonce-...'` in a comment is code, not prose, and stays as written.

## House style

- No serial (Oxford) comma before `and` / `or` in a list: `queues, services, staff and display mode`.
- A label and its value take a colon, not a dash: `Zola Clinic: front desk`, `Display mode: number only`.
- Sentences in body text end with a full stop; short UI fragments (buttons, badges, table cells) do not need one.
- Keep `aria-label` and `title` text punctuated like body text: screen readers read it aloud.

## Examples (from this codebase)

| Before | After |
|--------|-------|
| `the kernel version shows the destinations their grants make reachable —` | `the kernel version shows the destinations their grants make reachable:` |
| `Essential messages — account & security and financial notices — are always delivered` | `Essential messages (account & security and financial notices) are always delivered` |
| `Please raise a concern with us first — most are a misunderstanding` | `Please raise a concern with us first; most are a misunderstanding` |
| `{# Widgets — the example module's console. #}` | `{# Widgets: the example module's console. #}` |
| `“You're next — head inside”` | `"You're next, head inside"` |
| `Estimated wait 15-25 min` (web page) | `Estimated wait 15–25 min` |

## Checking

Run this before committing any template change; the only hits allowed are the placeholders and the
verbatim machine output described above:

```bash
grep -rnE "—|“|”|‘|’|[[:alnum:])\"'] - [[:alnum:]\"'(]| -- " src/templates
```
